+# ATTACK.md — red team, loop `attack`, round 0
+
+Target: `parseCsvLine` in `src/csv.mjs` (working-tree version, lines 18–81),
+judged against the contract in `README.md` lines 16–35.
+Runtime: Node v25.2.1. `npm test` passes 16/16 before the attack.
+
+Result: **no reproducible failure found**. `traces/` exists and is empty.
+
+## Method
+
+All attacks were run inline with `node --input-type=module -e '...'` from the
+project root (no scratch files were written). Four independent lines of attack:
+
+### 1. Differential fuzz against an independent reference parser
+
+A character-at-a-time state machine (`start | unquoted | in-quote | after-quote`)
+was written directly from README lines 21–35, sharing no code with `src/csv.mjs`.
+Outputs were compared: equal field arrays, or both throwing `CsvError`.
+
+- Exhaustive: every string of length 0..8 over the alphabet `"` `,` `\n` `\r` `a`
+  — 488,281 inputs, 0 mismatches. This covers every contract line for
+  separators, quoting, `""` escapes, what may follow a closing quote, unclosed
+  quotes, stray quotes, the single trailing `\n`/`\r\n` terminator, lone `\r`
+  in every position, `\r\n` split across quote boundaries, and empty text.
+- Random: 300,000 strings of length 0..29 over a 21-symbol alphabet including
+  `\r\n` as a unit, `""` as a unit, space, tab, NUL, an emoji surrogate pair,
+  lone high and low surrogates, U+0085, U+2028, backslash and `__proto__`
+  — 0 mismatches.
+
+### 2. Non-string input (README line 19)
+
+`undefined, null, 0, NaN, true, {}, [], ["a"], new String("a"), Symbol, function,
+10n, Object.create(null)`, an object with `toString`, an object with
+`Symbol.toPrimitive`, and a `Proxy` whose `get` trap throws. All threw
+`TypeError`; nothing coerced. The typeof guard at `src/csv.mjs:19-21` runs
+before any property access, so the Proxy trap never fires.
+
+### 3. Literal characters and result shape (README lines 31, 34–35)
+
+BOM, NBSP, U+2028/U+2029, NEL, VT, FF, RS, US, NUL, control chars, prototype-ish
+field names (`__proto__`, `constructor`, `length`, ...) all came back as literal
+fields in a plain `Array` (prototype `Array.prototype`) of strings. `CsvError`
+is a subclass of `Error` with `name === "CsvError"` and a stack (README line 17).
+Lone surrogates after a closing quote or after a stray quote produce `CsvError`;
+`JSON.stringify` in the message at `src/csv.mjs:60` does not throw on them.
+
+### 4. Performance and pathological shapes (README lines 18–19)
+
+26 shapes at 100 KB (102,400 code units), each timed once:
+all quotes (even and odd count), all `""` escapes, all commas, one huge quoted
+field, one huge unquoted field, many tiny quoted fields, many tiny escaped
+fields, `",` alternation, all `\r`, all `\r\n`, all `\n`, quoted `\r`/`\r\n`
+runs, all lone surrogates, all emoji, all spaces, all NUL, unclosed field of
+escapes, trailing stray quote, trailing lone `\r`, junk after closing quote,
+many fields then `\r`, quoted fields ending in `\n`, big field plus terminator,
+even quotes plus `\n`. Worst case: 8.7 ms (`a,` x 51,200 + `\r`). Every result
+was an array of strings or a `CsvError`; nothing else was thrown.
+
+Beyond the contract, 10 MB shapes (commas, escapes, single field, tiny quoted
+fields) completed in 28–240 ms with no non-`CsvError` exception, so there is
+no super-linear path reachable at scale either.
+
+## Why the code holds (source citations)
+
+- `src/csv.mjs:26-31` strips exactly one trailing `\n` or `\r\n` before parsing.
+  The comment at lines 23–25 is correct: a stripped terminator that was inside
+  an open quote leaves that quote unclosed either way, so the answer is
+  `CsvError` under both readings; the exhaustive sweep confirms no divergence.
+- `src/csv.mjs:41-42` bounds every `indexOf` by `end`, so a quote inside the
+  stripped terminator region cannot be matched (no such quote can exist anyway).
+- `src/csv.mjs:46` checks `q + 1 < end` before reading the escape partner, so
+  a `""` cannot straddle `end`.
+- `src/csv.mjs:54-61` admits only `,` or end after a closing quote; `\n`, `\r`,
+  space, tab and any other code unit fall to the `CsvError` at line 59.
+- `src/csv.mjs:67-75` rejects `"`, `\n`, `\r` in unquoted fields, and
+  `src/csv.mjs:76-77` yields the final (possibly empty) field, giving `[""]`
+  for empty text and `["a", ""]` for `a,`.
+- Both branches advance `i` or `j` monotonically and call `indexOf` from a
+  strictly increasing start, so the whole parse is O(n) with no rescans.
+
+## Verdict
+
+pass — no new failing trace.
