+# Changes
+
+## Round 0
+
+Traces fixed: none (no traces/ yet; this round implements the contract).
+
+### src/csv.mjs
+
+Rewrote `parseCsvLine` as a single-pass, index-based parser that implements
+every line of README.md § Contract:
+
+- Non-string input throws `TypeError` (unchanged).
+- Fields are separated by `,`; empty text is `[""]`, `a,` is `["a", ""]`.
+- Quoted fields: `""` inside quotes is one `"`; commas, `\n`, `\r\n` (and any
+  other character) inside quotes are literal.
+- After a closing quote only `,`, the record terminator or end of text may
+  follow; anything else is a `CsvError`. An unclosed quote is a `CsvError`.
+- A `"` outside quotes (anywhere but the first character of a field) is a
+  `CsvError`.
+- Whitespace outside quotes is kept.
+- One trailing `\n` or `\r\n` is stripped up front; any other unquoted `\r`
+  or `\n` is a `CsvError`.
+- Every other character (tabs, control characters, NUL, any Unicode, lone
+  surrogates) is literal.
+- Only `CsvError` (or `TypeError` for non-strings) is ever thrown; there is no
+  recursion and no per-character string slicing, so nothing can hang. The old
+  `rest.slice(1)` loop was O(n^2); the new parser is O(n).
+
+### tests/csv.test.mjs
+
+Added one test per contract line, plus:
+
+- a 100 KB timing test covering ten shapes (many quoted fields, one huge
+  unquoted/quoted field, all escaped quotes, all commas, quoted CRLFs, and
+  four erroring inputs), each asserted under 1 s;
+- a seeded fuzz test (20 000 short strings over a hostile alphabet) asserting
+  the result is always a non-empty array of strings or a `CsvError`.
